### B&M backend — IntelliJ HTTP Client
### Run any request with the green ▶ gutter icon.
### Pick the environment (prod/qa) from the dropdown next to ▶,
### values come from http-client.env.json.

### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/health

> {%
    client.test("health is up", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 200, "expected 200");
    });
%}

### Upload a price-proposal PDF (full chain: backend -> Docling OCR -> Postgres)
### Requires an admin Firebase ID token: set `firebaseIdToken` in
### http-client.private.env.json (never commit it). Adjust the file path as needed.
### Returns 201 when stored, or 200 "already up to date" when identical bytes were
### uploaded before (re-uploading a changed PDF with the same name replaces it).
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/upload-price-proposal
Authorization: Bearer {{firebaseIdToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----BMBoundary

------BMBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="table1.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../../Facturas/Precios Total/table1.pdf
------BMBoundary--

> {%
    client.test("upload accepted", function () {
        client.assert(response.status === 201 || response.status === 200, "expected 201/200, got " + response.status);
        client.assert(response.body.success === true, "success should be true");
    });
%}

### Fetch stored price-table results
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/price-table-results
